# des.bin

A studio site using the systemic architecture of
[abhibny/portfolio](https://github.com/abhibny/portfolio) and the measured visual
language of [Office Commun](https://officecommun.com/).

## Run locally

Requires Node.js 20.9 or newer.

```powershell
npm.cmd install
npm.cmd run dev
```

Open http://localhost:3000. If that port is busy, run
`npm.cmd run dev -- --port 3001`.

```powershell
npm.cmd run build
```

The production static site is generated in `out/`. Preview it with
`npm.cmd run preview` (or `npm.cmd start`) at http://localhost:3000.

## Structure

- `pages/`: homepage, Services, About, Contact, static project routes and 404.
- `components/`: shared shell, navigation, project cards and text rows.
- `data/studio.js`: studio text, service descriptions and project collection.
- `styles/globals.css`: measured typography, spacing, layout and responsive rules.
- `public/images/`: original dummy SVG graphics. No runtime image requests.
- `scripts/generate-placeholders.mjs`: regenerate graphics with `npm.cmd run assets`.
- `docs/reference.md`: measured values and architecture provenance.

All projects, descriptions, pricing choices and contact details are illustrative.
The contact form is connected to the configured Formspree endpoint. Booking links lead to the Contact page until a
real calendar URL is supplied.

To add real projects, edit `data/studio.js` and replace the local cover,
hero, mark, detail and web SVGs for each slug. Project pages, homepage cards,
service examples and next-project navigation read from the same collection.

For GitHub Pages under a repository subpath, set `NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH` before
building, for example `$env:NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH='/desbin'`. Internal links and
local asset paths respect that value. Leave it unset for a root domain.

Source repository: https://github.com/abhibny/desbin.
GitHub Pages deployment runs automatically on pushes to `main` through
`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`. The build uses the Pages base path so links,
fonts and illustrations work under `/desbin/`.

## Email enquiries

The form is configured with `https://formspree.io/f/xeaadyye` in
`data/studio.js`. It works with the existing React AJAX submission handler and
static export; no extra Formspree SDK or application server is required.

Set and verify the recipient inbox in your Formspree dashboard. Optionally copy
`.env.example` to `.env.local` to override `NEXT_PUBLIC_FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT` or set
`NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL` to the real address to display. Restart development
after changing environment values, or rebuild and redeploy the static site.

These public values are embedded at build time. No inbox password or private
API key belongs in the site. Formspree controls the recipient inbox; changing
the displayed email does not change where enquiries are delivered.

Submissions contain name, email (for replies), selected services, budget and
message. The form shows success only after Formspree accepts the request,
prevents duplicate submissions while sending, and retains entries on failure.
A hidden honeypot field is included. Enable additional spam protection and
allowed-domain restrictions in Formspree as appropriate for the deployed site.

To verify delivery, send a clearly labelled test enquiry from the configured
site and check both Formspree's submissions dashboard and the recipient inbox.
A successful HTTP response confirms acceptance, not final inbox delivery.
